course: dictionary
lesson: 10565
title: Opposites with un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The start un- often means undo or reverse. Uncoil is the reverse of coil: to coil is to wind something into rings, and to uncoil is to unwind it so it straightens out again. A rope, a hose or a snake can uncoil.
explain: Look at the context to check your idea. «Mother Jaguar's rule: when you find a Hedgehog you must drop him into the water and then he will uncoil.» The Hedgehog is curled up, and dropping him in the water makes him open out. So uncoil means unwind or straighten.
explain: Context can also tell you what a creature is doing. In «The Elephant's Child», the Bi-Coloured-Python-Rock-Snake uncoils himself from the rock. He is not just moving: he is unwinding his long body so he can go somewhere. Snakes coil to rest and uncoil to move or strike.
fact: The prefix un- often means undo or reverse, as in untie, unlock and uncoil.
fact: Uncoil means to unwind or straighten something that was wound into rings.
fact: Things that can uncoil include ropes, hoses and snakes.
fact: «Uncoil» is a verb, so its forms are uncoil, uncoils, uncoiled and uncoiling.
fact: Sailors uncoil ropes before they use them on a boat.
exercise: «Drop a Hedgehog in the water so he uncoils.» What does uncoils mean here? | Hides under a stone | Jumps out of the water | Sinks to the bottom of the pond | *Unwinds from a tight curl
exercise: The sailor must ___ the rope before the boat can leave the harbour. Which word fits best? | sink | coil up | hide | *uncoil
exercise: Find and copy the word that is the opposite of coil in this sentence: «The snake will coil to rest and uncoil to strike.» | snake | strike | *uncoil | rest
test: «The Bi-Coloured-Python-Rock-Snake uncoils himself from the rock.» What does uncoils mean? | *Unwinds and straightens out | Falls asleep | Climbs up onto the rock | Changes colour
test: The prefix un- in uncoil means what? | Again and again | Very large | Under the ground | *Reverse or undo
exam: Mother Jaguar says, «you must drop him into the water and then he will uncoil». Which choice shows the best use of context to work out uncoil? | Water always makes animals sleepy, so uncoil means yawn | The word has the letter u, so it must mean jump | Mother Jaguar is angry, so uncoil means shout | *The Hedgehog is curled up, so uncoil means unwinding
